From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brennoflavio <contato@brennoflavio.com.br>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 23:53:39 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] webapi: implement service-worker client claiming and
 controllers

Add a native, service-worker-only Clients object with stable identity and
claim(). Reject inactive workers with InvalidStateError without a nested
microtask checkpoint, allow claiming during activation, update controllers
without entering page JavaScript, queue trusted controllerchange events on
client schedulers, and queue claim-promise resolution on the worker scheduler.
Repeated claims leave unchanged controllers alone.

Discover document clients session-wide, including documents that never called
register() or accessed navigator.serviceWorker. Canonicalize creation URLs,
validate registration-scope origins, discard scope fragments, and use the
specification's serialized-URL longest-prefix matching after origin checks.
More-specific registrations win even while installing. Reuse page-realm
registration/ServiceWorker wrappers for controller identity.

Assign monotonically increasing session-local document IDs rather than using
reusable Frame addresses. Resolve IDs again at queued event delivery and
invalidate them before navigation/context reclamation, disconnected iframe
subtrees, and closed popup subtrees. Clear controllers when existing worker
registration detachment tears down their native scope. Scheduler finalizers
release pending claim resolvers and event task arenas on cancellation.

Validation:
- scripts/build.sh: passed.
- scripts/build.sh test: all 1658 existing tests passed unchanged.
- Ignored localhost HTTP/CDP fixtures with serviceworker explicitly enabled:
  activation waitUntil(clients.claim()), install InvalidStateError and
  synchronous-statement/microtask ordering, stable Clients identity and realm
  exposure, undefined promise result, controller wrapper identity, trusted
  event and event-handler delivery, duplicate-claim suppression, non-registering
  and lazy-container clients, canonical scope URLs, more-specific installing
  registrations, out-of-scope/origin/session exclusions, and immutable creation
  URL after history changes all passed.
- Loaded removed iframes and descendants of closed popups stay unclaimed and
  receive no stale events. Queued-claim/removal checks and 15 close/navigation/
  iframe-reuse stress iterations passed; unregister clears controllers.
- One reviewer pass: fixed subtree invalidation and inactive-claim promise
  checkpoint findings, then rebuilt and reran full tests and diagnostics.
- No new upstream tests or benchmark changes; diagnostics remain uncommitted.

Boundary: in-memory document claiming only. Session plus origin is the current
storage boundary; partitioned storage keys are not introduced. Workers retain
existing creating-Page ownership and disappear with it. Existing simplified
unregister/script replacement still detaches registrations immediately; this is
not a full service-worker update/unregister pipeline. Automatic navigation
control, fetch interception, Client wrappers, client enumeration, extendable
message delivery and worker-to-page replies remain unsupported. Experimental
feature defaults, ready semantics and persona values are not expanded. This
intermediate patch does not claim benchmark completeness or success.

Specification references:
https://w3c.github.io/ServiceWorker/#clients-claim
https://w3c.github.io/ServiceWorker/#notify-controller-change-algorithm
https://w3c.github.io/ServiceWorker/#scope-match-algorithm
